{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart during deployment can falsely block future deploys or leave a rolled-back deployment unreported."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A deployment job that hangs or disappears without writing status leaves subsequent automatic deploys stuck until the daemon restarts."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A documented port override can be lost when launching the deploy job, causing it to contact the wrong port and fail or affect another daemon."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A credential printed by a deployment command is persisted in the log without redaction."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After a connection interruption, the Land page can show stale information until its next poll, at most 15 seconds later."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"On an unsupported deployment platform, the configuration error is reported at deploy time rather than at startup."}]}